# tally 2.2.1 R21 (#221, 221.3), L §8.2 `unknown day:`: "`added <entry> of <calendar>` for a calendar's entry": two
# calendars with equal added entries print two lines. tally 2.2 printed one line, `added one_of([…])`.
# tally 2.3 (G1, #247): a window that reaches a move's `on` or `at` makes it a hole day (L §4.4 A movement takes a
# day, §5.14): the movement's places are the hole on every day, HOLE-IMPRECISE naming the day; re-stored.
=== cal2.tally
model cal2
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-10
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source card "invented"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place sav: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input pay: money PLN
input cal: calendar
input cal2: calendar
input from_day: date
move pay_cal: transfers
  on add_business(from_day, 1, cal)
  leg cash from world to sav amount pay
move pay_cal2: transfers
  on add_business(from_day, 1, cal2)
  leg cash from world to sav amount pay
version v_card
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  pay = 100.00 PLN "c"
  cal = calendar(weekends [sat, sun], added [one_of([2026-06-22, 2026-06-24])]) "c"
  cal2 = calendar(weekends [sat, sun], added [one_of([2026-06-22, 2026-06-24])]) "c"
  from_day = 2026-06-19 "c"
  opening[sav] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "c"
ask q1: bal(sav, 2026-06-22)
=== expect
q1: ?"date within window(2026-06-22, 2026-06-23) not precise enough for the day of pay_cal" (cal) ?"date within window(2026-06-22, 2026-06-23) not precise enough for the day of pay_cal2" (cal2)
  unknown day: added one_of([2026-06-22, 2026-06-24]) of cal
  unknown day: added one_of([2026-06-22, 2026-06-24]) of cal2
  cut 2026-01-10
